//  Regression guard: `string` is an aggregate, but the VM marshals it along its
//  own path (copy the text, pass a pointer plus a length), so it has to keep
//  crossing a native boundary. A check that rejected aggregates by value across
//  the boundary once caught `string` too, and the standard library's io would
//  not compile at all.
library "nowhere";
function describe(string text, ptr char buffer, int capacity):int;

function main():void { pass; eof: pass; }
